A||||18||Black88GT||3.4 GT vs. Eclipse GS-T (long racing story)||||6||
Z||000000||Black88GT||11-24-2000||09:39 PM||||<B>ROUND 1</B><P>I was headed to work today around 4 in the afternoon, so traffic was kind of heavy.  Well the way it works around here is like traffic travels in "packs" due to the way the lights change.  Well I just merged onto this road and I just beat a "pack" that was waiting at the light, so I was the leader. I was going pretty fast so I caught up to the next pack. As I was approaching the next pack I see this red Eclipse merge onto the same road.  I thought to myself...(homer)(homer) "hmmmmmm rice".  So I get in the far right lane of the 3 lane road to pass someone in the middle lane.  I notice the Elcipse follow, then this sucker mom in an SUV cuts me off, so he goes from the middle lane behind me, to the right lane behind me, then goes around me after this SUV cuts me off.  I figured I would follow his lead, and I did.  The red Eclipse gains some ground since I was slow in switching lanes.  He gets stuck behind some slow traffic too so I had a chance to catch up.  Here was my chance to get a better look at what I was up against.   Here is what I could tell from the exterior...<P><B>Newer Eclipse GS-T</B> ('95-'98?)<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE> <BR><LI>Eibach Springs (stock rims though)<BR><LI>Fart can exhaust (greddy according to sticker)<BR><LI>K&N Intake or Filter, not sure (just had K&N sticker)<BR><LI>EIP sticker also (upgraded turbo?)<BR></UL> <P><BR><B>My Fiero</B><BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE> <BR><LI>almost fully loaded (i.e. heavy)<BR><LI>stock 3.4 from '95 Camaro<BR><LI>Ported Manifolds<BR><LI>Borla exhaust with Dickman cat. elim. pipe<BR><LI>EVERYTHING else stock 2.8, injectors/fuel system - air filter - ignition - EVERYTHING.<BR></UL> <P>So anyway, we are in the middle lane now behind more slow traffic.  The right lane has an exit to another road, and the 5 cars clogging it up get off at the exit.  He swings over immediately and floors it.  There were about 3 rows of cars ahead of me and by the time I switched lanes he was already ahead of them, so in other words I was slow on the lane changing like before.  I figured I would try to catch up to him for the hell of it.  I wasn't really sure how I would fare but I haven't had a chance to go to the track or dyno it so here was my  chance. I remember when my brother had a GST for a short period of time and that thing was fast (but this was like 3 yrs ago when I thought anything faster then my moms car was unreal).  I was in 3rd gear doing about 45 when I switched lanes.  I floored it coming up the right hand lane passing all the cars ahead of us.  I was actually picking up some lost ground.  I shifted at about 5500 RPM and I stayed even with him the rest of the way, I didn't look at the speedo but the good old headlight door came up and last time that happened was at 110-120 so I am guessing around there.<P>We started to approach a residential neighborhood so we both shut it down.  At the light I pulled up next to him and he either gave me the finger or thumbs up, I couldn't really tell because his window was deeply tinted.  I think it was thumbs up though.  As I said we approached a residential neighborhood so we didn't race at that light or anything.  I was surprised that I kept up with him.  I was thinking to myself I would like to race him at a light so I could get the jump, then try to hold it tough after his turbo spools up.<P><B>ROUND 2</B><P>I am coming home from work, same road. This time I am at the opposite side of the light, coming from the residential neighborhood to the open road.  I start off easy and (as usual) I get stuck behind some retard doing 5 under the limit.  It's dark at this time and you can really only tell the difference between a car and a truck.  Well I see this car come out from behind me to pass. Guess who it was??  The <I>same</I> Eclipse that I had raced 5 hours earlier!  I heard the ring bell go off (ding ding) as I started to follow.  This time was just like the last time, I was gaining ground until I shifted into 4th where I stayed about the same.  We approached the light and I pull up right next to him.  Let's settle this I yelled out of the window.  He reved up in agreement.  The light turns green and I got a GREAT launch, minimal wheel spin and I was gone.  He was spinning for a second or two before I saw him start to catch up in my rearview.  I was shifting as fast as I could through second, then to third.  He was right at my door at this point.  I shifted into fourth where he gained that half car back and we were almost dead even.  We were at about 100 by this time and the light ahead of us was red.  He didn't say anything though.  I reved up again, ready for round 3, but then I noticed he had his blinker on.  I couldn't see the expression on his face though because his windows were tinted but I think he was mad because he didn't even look in my direction.<P>So that was my Friday racing story.  While it wasn't a kill or anything, it was the first time I got to test out my modifications against something other then a slow ricer Civic.  Needless to say I was pretty happy.<P>I feel that with 3.4 injectors, high volume fuel pump, adj. fuel pressure regulator,<BR>K&N filter (to replace my dirty one), and performance ignition, I would have had him.<BR>Add forced induction to all of that and he would have been eating my dust....<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">                         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">                       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">                     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">                         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif">        <P><p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 11-24-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||Shaun41178||11-25-2000||12:35 AM||||Wait to hang with that Eclipse from a roll.  Man the luck you get there and even better on the way home being the same car!!  Never happened to me before.<P>Way to crush the guy off the light.  I would call that one a kill.  After all you said you held him off till after 3rd gear.  Thrid gear in a Getrag is what 90 mph at 5500 rpm?  that is about a qtr mile or maybe a tad bit more.  Way to go man.  Streetracing is so much fun cause you never know what he otehr car might have.  If I had to guess I would think that the Eclipse had a 16G turbo or running more then stock boost on the stock turbo.  Those Eclipses are around 15.2 in the qtr stock.  If that Eclipse was modded then it could be in the mid 14's range.  AT worst I would say you have a low 15 second qtr mile car.  That is not too bad with todays standards.  Good enough to hang with Type R Integras stock.<P>Good kill and keep the racing stories coming.  Just be carefull at the same time.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>2.8 With nitrous<BR>Soon to have a 3.2 with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Performance</A>||||reg||10
Z||000002||HYPTNOTiSE||11-25-2000||01:07 AM||||Yeah baby! way to kick that ricers ass! Believe me folks jeff is just as crazy as he sounds from reading the story. It's funny i still recall that 5 at once lane change on the highway at 100+mph onto an exit ramp. See i'm vague on this part... did i almost piss my pants? or did I almost punch jeff in the jaw?  Can't remeber, probably both. Nice job dude, just think crane ignion and it would have been no contest <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||MikeE||11-25-2000||05:53 AM||||I agree that Jeff sounds crazy.  I often drive at around 4 in traffic with my 4 yr old daghter in the car and the last thing I need is some punk kids street racing up to 100mph endangering her life and everyone else's.  If you want to race, go to the track.<P>Otherwise, I can only hope that you get caught doing 100mph since you may have to sit in jail for awhile and think about it.  Your new insurance premium will have you thinking about it every month.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||11-25-2000||09:24 AM||||I see this one comming...Ya know, there is a HUGE difference between driving fast, and driving unsafely. One can be driving extremly fast and still be a very safe driver. On the other side, some one can be going 5 mph and be the biggest threat to you and your 4 year old daughter while your on the road. I dont have a problem with street racing, as long as its done in a safe manner, and your on a road that has two lanes (going in that same direction).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I think you could take him with the mods you mentioned above. There is a kid here with a 90 Eclipse, with Wal-Mart rims, all I know is that it is turbo. Has like 191K miles on it, AWD I think he said. He is just dieing to race me. I cant wait until I get my car all done with my 3.4. I was just waiting until some one posted here about a Turbo Eclipse, just to make sure I can take him before I get my balls in a up-roar. Nice Kill||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||11-25-2000||01:27 PM||||I figured someone would flame me, not like I care but I saw it coming from a mile away.<P>Racing the Eclipse was probably the best area to race.  I have been driving up and down this road for the past 4 years, never seen ANY pedestrians.  When we got to the residential area we both shut it down like I said.  It's not like I was going 130 mph down around a school.  <P>Why don't you come up here and lobby for a local track.  First you will have the county gov't telling you they don't have the money, then you will have the eco-nazi's telling you its bad for the enviroment.  No way would it ever happen.  The closest track to me is in a redneck county about 1 1/2 hours away.  <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||11-25-2000||01:38 PM||||Nice kill Jeff.<BR>And I totally agree with Sean's opinion on street racing. I think street racing can be done both safe and wreaklessly. It all depends on who's driving. <BR>Anyway's, I hate rice!<BR>NICE KILL!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||BBBAD GT||11-25-2000||09:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Why don't you come up here and lobby for a local track.  First you will have the county gov't telling you they don't have the money</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've never seen a county gov't own a racetrack before.  Is this normal in New England?  Just curious....<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||11-25-2000||11:53 PM||||You can't just build a racetrack.  You need county approval/permits.  Just like you can't just set up a store in the middle of a street or protest abortion whenever you feel like it.  You need permits.  I said County gov't because a friend of mine wanted to get a racetrack built on an area of county property but they sold it to some industrial business.  He had a bunch of local race shops willing to pitch in money and stuff, but they said they needed to sell it to an industrial site for more jobs and stuff.<P>Sorry I was mistaken in saying gov't but thats what made me say gov't.  My mistake...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff (always trying to blame something on the gov't lol)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 11-25-2000).]||||reg||1
