Z||000014||Black88GT||11-28-2000||08:59 AM||||I just saw the street where I was racing on the news! They said cops were cracking down on the street races on that strip.  They even showed a ricer race between a CRX and Celica.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||KnightRyder31||11-28-2000||07:56 PM||||Hell yes Pollock!!! I'll back you all the way!!<BR>Yeah, cops try to harrass me around here too.<BR>But I can handle it.||||reg||1
Z||000016||MikeE||12-03-2000||01:52 AM||||I don't care if you single me out or call me a whiner.  You guys may not care but you probably will when you kill a little kid and you have to face the distraught parents and explain why it was so important to prove a point to some guy in a rice burner.  You'll think about it for the rest of your life.  Jeff, it doesn't matter if there are no pedestrians.  If you had to weave in and out of traffic you are endangering everyone out there.  Even if you are a skillfull driver, that doesn't mean you won't cause someone else to have an accident.  My point was that racing belongs on a racetrack where everyone knows the risk, is well prepared, and is willing to accept the consequenses.  However, there is protocall even on a racetrack.  If you are going to streetrace (which I know you will), do when and where there are no other cars around.  Not only will will it be safer for others, you won't have some mom in an SUV cutting you off.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000017||RaeQwan||12-03-2000||03:36 AM||||let me say something here, I'm sure I got something smart to say. Just gimmie a second to think. I'll back sean up on that first comment he made. streetracing is as safe as the people who are particapating in it. Sure maybe some crazy a&& mom in a big as hell SUV might pull out in front of ya and cut ya off, is that the person who is racing fault? Not in my book, thats the SUV's fault. <B>Failing to yeild for oncoming traffic.</B><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwancfa.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||GT Bastard||12-03-2000||10:39 AM||||I can't say I agree with the weaving around in traffic.  I do almost all of my street racing after 1am in the morning when there is almost no other cars, or else we take it to a deserted country road(freshly paved) a couple miles outside of town.  All a person can really say is: Use common sense||||reg||1
